// PORT-PENDING 0968 tests-authority-manifest-module-group: tests/ban_bare_panic.rs:1-682
// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! W4 (durability, card #453): bans a bare `panic!(` in compiler-crate source
//RS //! outside an explicit, commented allowlist. Every real internal-compiler-bug
//RS //! panic site should go through `jet_foundation::ice!` (the single I2 banner
//RS //! macro, `crates/jet-foundation/src/Diagnostics.rs`) instead of a bare
//RS //! `panic!`, so every ICE reads the same. The allowlist below covers the only
//RS //! legitimate bare-`panic!` classes left:
//RS //!   - the `ice!` macro's own implementation (it must literally say `panic!`)
//RS //!   - `#[cfg(test)]`/`#[test]`-only assertion fixtures (never reached by a
//RS //!     real compile; a test failing loudly with `panic!` is normal Rust)
//RS //!   - the Prelude runtime templates (`Prelude/Core.rs`, `Layout.rs`,
//RS //!     `Scheduler.rs`) — these are `include_str!`-embedded text compiled into
//RS //!     the USER's program, not compiler code; their panics are the `jet_panic`
//RS //!     runtime-panic path (`RUNTIME_PANIC` = 70), a different contract than I2.
//RS //!   - the scheduler host bindings (`SchedulerHost.rs`): `#[cfg(test)]`
//RS //!     assertion fixtures only.
//RS //!
//RS //! A file not on the allowlist may have zero bare `panic!`s. A file on the
//RS //! allowlist may have AT MOST its listed count — so both a brand new bare
//RS //! panic site AND a seeded extra panic on an already-allowlisted file trip
//RS //! this test, per card #453's exit criteria.
//RS //!
//RS //! CI and `Tools/agent/verify-full.sh` pick this root integration target up
//RS //! through the complete Cargo test-target inventory. Run:
//RS //! `Tools/agent/jet-env cargo test --test ban_bare_panic`
